  "question": {
    "text": "A variable line through the point <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math> cuts the coordinate axes at the points <math><mi>A</mi></math> and <math><mi>B</mi></math> respectively. If the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> divides <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> internally in the ratio <math><mn>2</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo></math> then the equation of the locus of <math><mi>P</mi></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
